# {{PROJECT_NAME}} — design contract

<!-- trailhead v{{VERSION}} -->

**Conformance is composition, not palette.** A page that applies the correct color and
type tokens to a layout arrived at independently is *not* conformant. It will be
internally consistent, it will pass every automated token check, and it will be lifeless.
That exact outcome is why this file exists: a build with a pinned design system and a
46KB token extraction shipped pages using none of the system's compositional patterns,
and nothing in its specification would have failed it.

So the mapping table below is a **precondition, not a record**. The row for a surface is
written *before* the surface is built, naming the source pattern it is an application of.
Filled in afterwards, it documents what happened rather than constraining what happens —
and `scripts/checks/surface-mapping.mjs` flags a surface file newer than this contract
for that reason.

